{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Cancel Effects","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},{"text":" and the store’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"all-or-nothing","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" effect or the imperative ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" method. Identity lives outside the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Choosing an id","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" to tag the work, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to stop it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancelInFlight: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancels any effect already running under the id ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".queryChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Cancel from view or scene code","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"What it does not replace","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" continuation should still release it — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"defer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"else","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" has to stop the effect early.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","title":"Add a Parental Gate","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add a Paywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","title":"Add Analytics","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancel(id:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","abstract":[{"text":"An effect that cancels every in-flight effect running under ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"